Psalm 119:17-24

17 Déal bóuntifully with your sérvant,
that I may líve and kéep your wórd.
18 Ópen my éyes, that I may sée
the wónders of your láw.

19 I am a pílgrim in the lánd;
híde not your commánds from me.
20  My sóul is consúmed with lónging
at áll tímes for your decrées.

21 You thréaten the próud, the accúrsed,
who stráy from your commánds.
22 Frée me from scórn and contémpt,
for I obsérve your decrées.

23 Though prínces sit plótting agáinst me,
your sérvant pónders your státutes.
24 Sée, your decrées are my delíght;
your státutes are my cóunselors.

Glóry to the Fáther, and to the Són,
and to the Hóly Spírit:
as it wás in the begínning, is nów,
and will be for éver. Amén.
